; Anomaly Coop - vehicles for players: the passenger places of each car section (F5-VEH-5, build 58, docs/VEHICLES.md sections 4 and 12).
; Read once per process by every process (both modes): the decider seats players by these places (coop_vehicles_seat.cpp), a
; player's machine sits its actor there (coop_vehicles_ride.cpp). The same file on every machine: a seat a machine does not know is
; given back (the player asks out). The parser and its tests: engine/src/xrCoop/coop_vehicle_seats.h, tests/test_vehicle_seats.cpp.
;
;   seats  = n                    places with the driver's (seat 0, the stock place: car_definition driver_place), 1..8.
;                                 No section or no line: the driver alone.
;   seat_<i> = <bone>[, <dx, dy, dz>][, <yaw>]   a bone of the model ("driver": the driver's place), moved in the car's space
;                                 (x right, y up, z forward, metres), turned by <yaw> degrees about its up axis (positive: to the right)
;   seat_<i> = <x, y, z>, <yaw>   a point in the car's space, the car's axes turned by <yaw>
;   exit_<i> = left | right | back   where the passenger stands up (beside the car's box); no line: the side the seat is on
;   eye    = x, y, z              optional: the passenger's eye in his seat's space; no line: the driver's camera (camera_pos) over his
;                                 seat, else 0, 0.75, 0.1
; A missing or malformed seat_<i> ends the places before it; every problem is written to the log once, with the section.
;
; The car sections are those of the stock configs\vehicles.ltx (class SCRPTCAR; GAMMA's configs define no others): grok_vehicles_spawner
; places veh_tr13, veh_zaz_968, veh_niva, veh_uaz_01, veh_uaz_02, veh_kamaz, veh_zaz; the tm_military quest places veh_btr.
; The numbers are estimates from the models' user data (configs\models\vehicles\*.ltx: driver_place, camera_pos - the driver's eye,
; x < 0 is his side) and the cars' sizes. Nobody has seen them in game yet: the lead checks them on the stand with screenshots.
; Most places are given from the driver's place, so a seat moves with it if a model's driver_place moves.

; VAZ-2121 Niva, 2 doors, 4 places: the driver (camera_pos x -0.4), the front passenger mirrored, the rear bench
[veh_niva]
seats  = 4
seat_1 = driver, 0.8, 0, 0
exit_1 = right
seat_2 = driver, 0.05, 0.05, -0.85
exit_2 = left
seat_3 = driver, 0.75, 0.05, -0.85
exit_3 = right

